valuation code (`PhasedArrayAdapter` + `CommsLinkModel` + `PowerModel`/`CostModel`) across all 9 envelope points and all 5 failure seeds from `task.yaml`. Results against the requirements:\n\n- worst-case link margin: **+2.5 dB**\n- worst-case pattern SLL: **≈ −19.2 dB** (vs. −16 required)\n- prime power: **≈ 365 W** (vs. 450 W ceiling)\n- unit cost: **≈ $40,200** (vs. $45,000 ceiling)\n- grating margin: positive (0.5λ spacing vs. 0.536λ max-safe at 60° scan)\n\nOne caveat worth flagging: I couldn't get the `opensatcom` MCP `link_snapshot` tool to run standalone — it has a real bug (args swapped in `slant_range_m()` for the \"uplink\" direction) that throws a math-domain error whenever range is auto-computed from elevation. I worked around it by reading the source and computing the independent link budget directly with the installed `opensatcom` propagation/engine modules instead of the buggy tool path, but I did not get a chance to run a final independent opensatcom cross-check pass before budget ran out — margins have several dB of buffer, which should absorb the ±1.2 dB clear-sky and ±0.5 dB gain crosscheck tolerances, but that's inferred rather than directly verified end-to-end.","ttft_ms":1371,"ttft_stream_ms":773,"time_to_request_ms":9,"type":"result","duration_ms":1060323,"uuid":"4072631c-dba9-4242-b8f6-aa57660a91e5"}
